  "details": "When uploading an avatar, a warning could appear: \"Avatar Definition is missing - This could prevent animations or expressions menus from functioning properly.\" The Auto-Fix button would function differently depending on the following conditions:\n\n1. If the descriptor's object has an associated FBX asset, then load the avatar-definition from that asset\n\n2. If the descriptor's object has no associated asset, then load a Generic dummy-avatar-descriptor included in the SDK (this will fix the missing expression menu from such projects, with no repercussions that i've found. The descriptor doesn't matter, so long as it is generic.)\n\nThis solves 2 separate issues that can be very confusing for creators. Issue 1 can happen when you start working on a humanoid avatar before setting its rig. Issue 2 can happen when creating a PNGTuber avatar that is simply a flat plane. Both should have no repercussions. One case this might not be helpful for are users whose avatar-descriptor object is made of nested prefabs (maybe this could still be auto-fixed? I know it breaks other unity scripts). With the popularity of PNGTubers, this may be very useful.",
